  "description": "De Hallen Amsterdam is a cultural centre and national heritage site in Amsterdam’s Oud-West district, where art, film, craftsmanship and community come together.\nFrom exhibitions to talks, cinemas to makerspaces – De Hallen is a vibrant meeting place for urban culture, creativity and social enterprise. \nLocated in a former tram depot, the complex houses independent galleries, workshops, markets, the renowned FilmHallen cinema and the popular Foodhallen – all part of a larger cultural ecosystem.",
